{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Staintopoletan and the ruler of the County of Tripoli. He was the son of Pons of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was born in 1152 and succeeded his father in 1187. He was a skilled military leader and politician who played a key role in the Third Crusade.\n\n* **Early Life and Succession** *\nRaymond III was born in 1152 to Pons of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was a member of the royal family of Jerusalem and had a significant influence on Raymond's early life. After the death of his father in 1187 Raymond III succeeded him as the Count of Tripoli.\n\n* **Relationship with Saladin** *\nRaymond III had a complex relationship with Saladin the Sultan of Egypt and Syria. Despite being on opposite sides of the conflict Raymond III and Saladin had a deep respect for each other's military skills and chivalry. In 1187 Raymond III was captured by Saladin's forces after the Battle of Hattin. He was later released in 1188 after the payment of a ransom.\n\n* **Third Crusade** *\nDuring the Third Crusade Raymond III allied himself with King Richard the Lionheart of England. He played a key role in the Crusader victory at the Battle of Arsuf in 1191. Raymond III also participated in the Siege of Acre but was forced to withdraw due to a lack of resources.\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 but some sources suggest that he may have died in 1199. His death led to a succession crisis in the County of Tripoli which was eventually resolved by the appointment of Bohemond IV of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob"